  "content": "# =============================================================================
# AutoCell 7nm (tcbn7) Example - CAD Layers (1/7)
#
# Declares the physical layers (and their functions / GDS stream mapping, via
#
# foundry deck declares ~1700 layers (analog/RF/SRAM/MOM/ESD/TSV, the whole
# M3-M17 stack, etc.); here it is trimmed to only the 7nm FinFET stack this
# place-&-route flow builds, so the technology stays self-contained and light.
#
# The layers below are the ones referenced by the design rules (rules.tcl), the
# placement templates / boundary / device classes (place.tcl), the routing grids
# and pin template (route.tcl), the via stacks (viadefs.tcl) and the layer
# coloring (rules.tcl).  Each layer's *function* (its semantic role - poly,
# nwell, nplus/pplus, m1/m2, contacts, vias, etc.) is carried over unchanged
# from the foundry deck (library/tech.tcl).
#
# IC context (see doc/knowledge/design-rules-glossary.md):
#   A bare GDS layer number only identifies a mask.  The layer set here is the
#   7nm FinFET stack: OD/PO/MP/MD (active, poly gate, gate metal, diffusion
#   metal), NW/PP/NP/VTL (wells & threshold implants), VD/VG + the cut layers
#   (CPO/CMD/CM1A/CM1B/CM2A/CM2B/V1/V2), M1/M2/M3 and their colour variants
#   (M1A/M1B, M2A/M2B, M3A/M3B for multi-patterning).  Layer *roles* drive
#   device recognition, contact landing and well/implant polarity during
#   extraction, DRC and LVS.
#
# =============================================================================

tech -process finfet
tech add_layer -name "BCM0:drawing5" -gds {180 165}
tech add_layer -name "BCM0:drawing6" -gds {180 166}
tech add_layer -name "BCMD" -gds {84 160}
tech add_layer -name "BVG" -gds {179 274}
tech add_layer -name "CCP:drawing1" -gds {98 1}
tech add_layer -name "CM1A" -gds {180 109}
