  "content": "# =============================================================================
# AutoCell 7nm (tcbn7) Example - Design Rules (5/7)
#
# The foundry manufacturing constraints that every drawn shape must satisfy:
# minimum width / spacing / area, plus conditional and colour-aware rules for
# multi-patterned metal layers (M1A/M1B, M2A/M2B, M3A/M3B).  Declared by the
# shipped deck (kept unmodified in library/); grouped here, together with the
# multi-patterning layer-coloring rules that drive them.
#
# IC context (see doc/knowledge/design-rules-glossary.md):
#   A design rule is "layer + geometric relationship + limit value", e.g. minimum
#   poly width = 0.008 um (PO), minimum M1 width = 0.020 um.  min_width is the
#   smallest a drawn shape may be; min_area the smallest legal polygon; and
#   min_spacing the smallest gap between shapes.  At 7nm the metal layers are
#   *coloured* (M1A/M1B ...) so that patterns split across masks, and the
#   colour-aware spacing rules below (SPACING_COLOR) enforce the intra/inter-mask
#   clearances.
# =============================================================================
